[
  {
    "number": 65,
    "title": "Package shared monitoring setup and Pixoo acceptance runbook",
    "body": "Pixoo monitoring had no pinned consumer rehearsal for the shared setup SDK. This change packages Hub #8's unchanged archive as a development dependency and tests it against the real Pixoo simulator, then documents the operator setup/removal and acceptance sequence.\n\nRefs #34. Source packaging can ship first; this PR does not close the issue. Personal installation, required-client qualification, Nanoleaf coexistence/cutover, physical observations and the Hub #6 frontend trial remain pending.\n\nValidation: Node 24.21.0 `npm ci` and `npm run check` pass, including 588 application tests and 10 workflow tests. After synchronization/archive, workflow checks pass with 18 current specifications and 19 archives. The new fixture covers enabled Codex/Claude sources, an unqualified disabled source, stale-plan rejection, repeated setup/removal, private backup, synthetic canary exclusion from returned state, unrelated-hook preservation and HTTP 401 after revocation. Linux/WSL only; the fixture explicitly skips native Windows.\n\nThe first meaningful red result was the missing shared package. Fixture corrections addressed startup credential provisioning, Vitest package resolution and the bound listener's Host requirement. No application runtime behavior changed. The 3.4 MiB upstream archive is development-only; its source/hash receipt and merged-source CI are recorded under vendor/.\n\nOpenSpec `gh-34-agent-monitoring-integration` is synchronized and archived. Independent Standards and Specification reviews and all five current-head CI jobs remain merge gates. Guide companion: https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/pull/131, owned by this delivery coordinator. Public guide publication is outside scope. No personal configuration, live client, state migration or physical device was changed.\n\nIndependent Standards and Specification review round 1 both report no P0-P3 findings for base `28f4875b7a0f0e57ca6f25d9971e125e927a5503` to head `e5bf74f4268bf3376686a3fc8b9afbe57c18f1ba`. Each used a separate read-only context, requested Astra/high. Runtime model identity and usage are unknown. Coordinator plus two reviewers used; no advisor consultations. Source packaging is approved within its boundary; full issue acceptance remains pending.\n",
    "state": "open",
